# generate-submission/SKILL.md is force-added and tracked despite this rule (git can't re-include
# a path via !negation once a parent directory is excluded — confirmed, that pattern doesn't work
# at any nesting depth). It survives via `git add -f`, not via a gitignore exception. Don't remove
# it from tracking; it's the single authoritative authoring-process definition, not local config.
